Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["7+1: the octonions and the Clifford algebra of 7+1 spacetime", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"2a937243-55e1-d147-87a6-922b08538b35"],

Cell["\<\
A real realization of the octonions and a real 16\[Times]16 realization of \
the Clifford algebra, built from \[LongDash] and mirroring \[LongDash] the \
split octonions and the 16\[Times]16 Dirac matrices of 4+4.nb\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"e5cbb4a1-2f41-1946-9db2-e2e60486438a"],

Cell["\<\
Prepared for Nash's 7+1 project (github.com/once-ere/7+1). Wolfram Language \
15.0.1. This notebook was generated by tools/make_7p1_nb.py and evaluated in \
Wolfram 15.0.1; every claim in it is checked by a cell of the form \
check[\"name\", test].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cd6eac5b-b618-494b-a73a-6ce7ce4a254b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Summary. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Starting from the real 8\[Times]8 matrices \[Tau][A] and the real \
16\[Times]16 Dirac matrices T16[A] of 4+4.nb (split octonions and the \
Clifford algebra Cl(4,4)), this notebook constructs: (i) a real realization \
of the octonions, \[Tau]O[A] = \[Tau][A] for A \[LessEqual] 3 and \[Tau]O[A] \
= \[Tau][A].\[Sigma] for A \[GreaterEqual] 4, whose multiplication table is \
produced by exactly the same vielbein formula as the split-octonion table of \
4+4.nb; (ii) the Clifford algebra of 7+1 spacetime (x0 = time = the octonion \
unit, x1 \[Ellipsis] x7 = space) as REAL 16\[Times]16 matrices \
\[CapitalGamma]17[A] built from T16; this is possible because the octonions\
\[CloseCurlyQuote] own quadratic form Re(x x) = x0\.b2 \[Minus] x1\.b2 \
\[Minus] \[Ellipsis] \[Minus] x7\.b2 has signature (1,7) and Cl(1,7) \
\[TildeFullEqual] \[DoubleStruckCapitalR](16); (iii) a proof that with the \
opposite overall sign (the sign convention of 4+4.nb, metric \[Eta]71) no \
real 16\[Times]16 realization exists, because Cl(7,1) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalH](8); for that convention the notebook gives the \
minimal complexification \[CapitalGamma]71 (the exact block form of T16 with \
a single factor i) and a real 32\[Times]32 realization; (iv) examples: Fano \
plane, Moufang identities, the eight-square identity, Cayley\[Dash]Dickson \
doubling, so(1,7), a boost and a rotation, the 7+1 Dirac operator, real \
on-shell spinor amplitudes, real massless and massive spinor fields, and the \
classification of all nine signatures p+q = 8. All checks are collected in \
the last section."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"22021729-425f-e94d-b840-75eb793218b0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["0. How to use this notebook", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e5161c5e-ba7d-7047-81d3-c7b905df4988"],

Cell["\<\
Evaluate the whole notebook in order (Evaluation \[RightPointer] Evaluate \
Notebook). Each verification is a cell check[\"name\", test]; it prints name \
\[RightArrow] True and stores the result in the association checks. Section 6 \
lists all checks; allChecksPassed must be True.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ae89d2a-1a8d-9b49-adc9-cc2c8fd66e46"],

Cell["\<\
The notebook has its own private context (CellContext \[RightArrow] \
Notebook), so its symbols cannot collide with the symbols of 4+4.nb (which \
protects, for example, unit and hUSE) when both notebooks are open.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5aa94e59-127d-2a47-aecc-0d32568148e7"],

Cell["\<\
Index conventions: A, B, K, L run over 0 \[Ellipsis] 7 and label the \
coordinates x0 \[Ellipsis] x7, the octonion units e[0] \[Ellipsis] e[7] and \
the generators \[CapitalGamma]17[0] \[Ellipsis] \[CapitalGamma]17[7]; i, j \
run over the imaginary/space values 1 \[Ellipsis] 7. Mathematica lists are \
1-based, hence the frequent [[A+1, B+1]]. The letters C, D, E, I, N, O are \
built-in Wolfram symbols and are never used as variables here.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ff7f6ea3-b8bc-a742-a969-cea50ceb237d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["{$Version, $Context}", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ba92bf9e-8ebf-9b44-816f-678514fc2f8f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"15.0.1 for Microsoft Windows (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Notebook$$43$40478`\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002040478815317*^9},
