Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1.4 The two definitions [1A] and [1B], and four corrections", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"4b85ff66-22d5-5640-b9d1-2d2f59d6c91c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["[1A] Octonions ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalO]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2e905d98-4f4e-634c-9b08-ad62b3f16189"],
 StyleBox[". ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "An 8-dimensional, non-associative, non-commutative normed division algebra \
over \[DoubleStruckCapitalR] with basis e[0] = 1, e[1], \[Ellipsis], e[7]; \
e[i]\.b2 = \[Minus]1 (i = 1 \[Ellipsis] 7); products of distinct imaginary \
units follow the oriented lines of the Fano plane, each line spanning a \
quaternion subalgebra. Conjugation x\:0304 = x0 \[Minus] \[CapitalSigma] xi \
e[i] is an anti-automorphism, (xy)\:0304 = y\:0304 x\:0304. Re(x) = (x + x\
\:0304)/2 = x0. Norm N(x) = x x\:0304 = x\:0304 x = x0\.b2 + \[Ellipsis] + x7\
\.b2, multiplicative: N(xy) = N(x) N(y). Inverse x\:207b\.b9 = x\:0304/N(x). \
Alternative: x(xy) = (xx)y, (yx)x = y(xx); power-associative. \
Cayley\[Dash]Dickson: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalO]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "18c6386d-d0ec-de41-9ab1-7e2c9fdb6cab"],
 " = \[DoubleStruckCapitalH] \[CirclePlus] \[DoubleStruckCapitalH] as pairs \
of quaternions."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"309a7507-14b4-694f-82cb-84559c7e58be"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["[1B] Clifford algebra of an 8-dimensional space. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Cl(V,Q) = T(V)/I_Q(V), with I_Q(V) the two-sided ideal generated by v\
\[CircleTimes]v \[Minus] Q(v)1. In the quotient v\.b2 = Q(v)1 and vw + wv = \
2B(v,w)1 with B(v,w) = (Q(v+w) \[Minus] Q(v) \[Minus] Q(w))/2. For an \
orthogonal basis e_A: e_A\.b2 = Q(e_A) and e_A e_B = \[Minus]e_B e_A (A \
\[NotEqual] B). Dimension 2^8 = 256, graded by binomial(8,k). Over \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalC] every signature gives Cl_8(\[DoubleStruckCapitalC]) \
\[TildeFullEqual] \[DoubleStruckCapitalC](16), acting on \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalC]^16 (complex Dirac spinors)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e2cf320d-8879-a64c-bd7f-239d776400db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Corrections found while verifying these definitions ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "(each is checked by a cell of this notebook):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cc21eec5-b97c-f046-b901-2327d989751f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "(1) The second Cayley\[Dash]Dickson formula of [1A], (a,b)(c,d) = (ac \
\[Minus] d\:0304b, \[ABar]d + cb), does NOT define the octonions: it is not \
alternative and its norm is not multiplicative (explicit counterexample in \
section 3.5). A correct formula of the same shape is (a,b)(c,d) = (ac \
\[Minus] d b\:0304, \[ABar] d + c b) (J. Baez, The Octonions, 2002, section \
2.2); the octonions of this notebook satisfy it exactly, with x = a + ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 " b and ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 " = e[4]. The first formula of [1A] contains a stray symbol \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]x\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and cannot be read \
unambiguously."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2d4c4851-2268-824d-bc87-9d9432274238"],

Cell["\<\
(2) The grade-4 dimension is binomial(8,4) = 70, not 72: 1 + 8 + 28 + 56 + 70 \
+ 56 + 28 + 8 + 1 = 256.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f1884e2e-4c42-9b48-9817-2f21a3151b90"],

Cell["\<\
(3) The classification table of [1B] is not correct for the stated relation v\
\.b2 = Q(v). With p = number of generators squaring to +1: Cl(8,0) \
\[TildeFullEqual] \[DoubleStruckCapitalR](16), Cl(7,1) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalH](8), Cl(6,2) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalH](8), Cl(5,3) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR](16), Cl(4,4) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR](16), Cl(3,5) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalH](8), Cl(2,6) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalH](8), Cl(1,7) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR](16), Cl(0,8) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR](16). \[DoubleStruckCapitalC](16) can never occur: it \
has real dimension 512, while every Cl(p,q) with p + q = 8 has real dimension \
256. Several \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Metric Signs\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
entries were also mistyped. Section 5.6 computes the whole table.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ef362de0-188c-8f44-afbd-0690b14f0f0d"],

Cell["\<\
(4) Split octonions are NOT a division algebra: they have zero divisors, e.g. \
(eA[1] + eA[5])(eA[1] \[Minus] eA[5]) = 0 in the table of 4+4.nb (section \
2.4). They are a composition algebra whose norm is indefinite, of signature \
(4,4).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"40c913b1-c1ab-b84f-8e85-268074503035"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Consequence for this project. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "With v\.b2 = Q(v) and the sign convention of 4+4.nb (Q = \[Eta]71), the \
Clifford algebra of 7+1 spacetime is Cl(7,1) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalH](8): no rearrangement of indices and no real change of \
basis can give real 16\[Times]16 matrices (proof in section 4.4). With the \
opposite overall sign (Q = \[Eta]17, the octonions\[CloseCurlyQuote] own \
quadratic form Re(x x)) the algebra is Cl(1,7) \[TildeFullEqual] \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR](16), and section 4.2 builds it from the real 4+4 \
matrices. Section 4.3 gives, for \[Eta]71, the complexification of the 4+4 \
matrices (one factor i), and section 4.5 a real 32\[Times]32 realization."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"770d07a2-003b-0d46-80a8-3cd0c65f4221"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Recap: the 4+4 objects, reproduced exactly from 4+4.nb", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"583e2e58-6eb0-a74a-a34b-5f22fdb132fb"],

Cell["\<\
Every definition in this section is copied from 4+4.nb (renamed only as in \
the dictionary of section 1.3). The checks repeat the checks of 4+4.nb; \
together they show that the 4+4 construction is remembered exactly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5511e15a-c435-964c-a8c2-134224145e71"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
2.1 \[Sigma], the self-dual and anti-self-dual blocks, \[Zeta], \[Tau] and \
\[Tau]bar\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"35428236-1ddb-7c49-814f-63057c513aba"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
\[Sigma] = ArrayFlatten[{{Zero4, ID4}, {ID4, Zero4}}];
Qa[h_, p_, q_] := Signature[{h, p, q, 4}];
Qb[h_, p_, q_] := ID4[[p, 4]]*ID4[[q, h]] - ID4[[p, h]]*ID4[[q, 4]];
SelfDualAntiSymmetric[h_, p_, q_] := Qa[h, p, q] - Qb[h, p, q];
AntiSelfDualAntiSymmetric[h_, p_, q_] := Qa[h, p, q] + Qb[h, p, q];
Do[s4by4[h] = Table[Table[SelfDualAntiSymmetric[h, p, q], {q, 4}], {p, 4}], \
{h, 1, 3}];
Do[t4by4[h] = Table[Table[AntiSelfDualAntiSymmetric[h, p, q], {q, 4}], {p, \
4}], {h, 1, 3}];
\[Zeta][0] = ID8;
Table[\[Zeta][7 - h] = ArrayFlatten[{{0, t4by4[h]}, {-t4by4[h], 0}}], {h, 1, \
3}];
Table[\[Zeta][h] = ArrayFlatten[{{0, s4by4[h]}, {s4by4[h], 0}}], {h, 1, 3}];
\[Zeta][7] = \[Zeta][1].\[Zeta][2].\[Zeta][3].\[Zeta][4].\[Zeta][5].\[Zeta][6];
\[Tau][0] = ID8; Do[\[Tau][A] = \[Zeta][A], {A, 1, 7}];
\[Tau]bar[0] = ID8; Do[\[Tau]bar[A] = \[Sigma].Transpose[\[Tau][A]].\[Sigma], \
{A, 1, 7}];
{Row[Table[MatrixForm[s4by4[h]], {h, 3}], \"  \"], \
Row[Table[MatrixForm[t4by4[h]], {h, 3}], \"  \"]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1426d39f-bb22-c348-aa61-c3c84c65794a"],

