Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
3.3 The octonion multiplication constants: gridO, the mirror of gridx\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b22bdbde-08a4-6a45-afd7-0818a9ee9346"],

Cell["\<\
Exactly as in 4+4.nb, the left multiplication by e[A] in the e-basis is LO[A] \
= gO[[A+1,A+1]] EO.\[Tau]O[A].EOinv, and e[A] e[K] = \[CapitalSigma]_L \
LO[A][[L+1, K+1]] e[L]. The basis is now 0-based, e[A] \[LeftRightArrow] \
\[Tau]O[A] \[LeftRightArrow] xA, so the index shift B\[Minus]1 of 4+4.nb \
disappears. The table is computed with the formula of gridx, letter for \
letter:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"be8e829f-b55b-8640-827f-d06ad8862403"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
eList = Array[e, 8, 0];
LO[A_] := LO[A] = FullSimplify[gO[[A + 1, A + 1]] EO.\[Tau]O[A].EOinv];
gridO = Grid[Partition[Flatten[{{{x}, eList}, Table[({{x}, \
FullSimplify[ExpandAll[gO[[B, B]] eList.EO.\[Tau]O[B - 1].EOinv]]} /. {x -> \
e[B - 1]}), {B, 1, 8}]}], 9], Frame -> All]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[94]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2a307f5a-043f-d348-8cab-2f238a94194f"],

